e brief). The above evidence SC Appeal 87/2017 10 shows that her claim for prescription to the property in question could not be accepted. For the aforementioned reasons, I hold that the learned Judges of the Civil Appellate High Court were wrong when they decided the case in favour the Defendant-Respondent. I hold that the learned District Judge was correct when he decided the case in favour of the Plaintiff-Appellant. For the above reasons, I set aside the judgment of the Civil Appellate High Court dated 6.6.2016 and affirm the judgment of the learned District Judge dated 5.12.2008. In view of the conclusion reached above, I answer the 2 nd,3rd and 4th questions of law in the affirmative. The 1st question of law does not arise for consideration. The Plaintiff-Appellant is entitled to costs in all three courts. Appeal allowed. Judge of the Supreme Court. Kumudini Wickramasinghe J I agree. Judge of the Supreme Court. Janak de Silva J I agree. Judge of the Supreme Court. SC Appeal 87/2017 11 

