 Pabhankara Thero. The deceased Plaintiff had proved the case against the Defendant on a balance of probability before the trial court. I hold therefore that the Court of Appeal had quite correctly come to the finding that prayer (a) to the Plaint should be granted as relief. I answer the questions of law enumerated above in the negative against the Appellant. I affirm the judgment of the Court of Appeal. The Appeal is dismissed. However I order no costs. Judge of the Supreme Court. H.N.J.Perera J. I agree. Judge of the Supreme Court. Vijith K. Malalgoda PCJ. I agree. Judge of the Supreme Court. 12 

